<Base title="Serial Port Interface TX9-TMR/2" description="Activate a turnstile, gate, door strike or mag lock from a PC serial port, or turn a Wiegand reader into a dry contact.">
  <div class="wrap prose" style="padding-bottom:72px">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/library/">Library</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>Serial Port Interface</nav>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.4rem);font-weight:800">Serial Port Interface</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A computer-controlled relay. Send any ASCII character to the PC's serial port and the relay activates your turnstile,
      gate operator, door strike or magnetic lock. Common in club management and parking garage systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>New:</strong> it can also turn a stand-alone Wiegand reader into a dry contact closure. No access control
      computer or software needed. It responds to all cards and fobs the reader recognizes, and supplies 12VDC to power the
      reader. Simple 2 to 4 wire hookup.
    </p>
    <p>Check with your software vendor that the authorization signal sends ASCII characters to the serial port. You need one interface and one serial port per controlled output.</p>
    <h2>Setup</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Connect your hardware to the Normally Open terminals (turnstiles, gate operators, fail-lock strikes) or Normally Closed terminals (fail-safe strikes, mag locks).</li>
      <li>Connect the DB9 connector to the PC's serial port. A USB to serial adapter works on computers without one.</li>
      <li>Connect the supplied arc suppression snubber capacitor across the terminals you're using.</li>
      <li>Plug the power supply into a 115VAC outlet.</li>
      <li>Set the timer: minimum for momentary-contact devices like turnstiles, or the desired hold-open time (up to about 1 minute) for strikes and mag locks without their own timer.</li>
    </ol>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/parts/tx9-tmr-2/">Order the TX9-TMR/2</a> <a href="/media/spi/spi-hookup.pdf" style="margin-left:12px">Hookup diagram (PDF)</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
